---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GrowthStage from '../components/GrowthStage.astro';
const stages = [
  {number:'01',stage:'Understand',image:'approach-understand.png',text:'Listen, observe, map the current state, and define the problem worth solving.'},
  {number:'02',stage:'Design',image:'approach-design.png',text:'Connect insights, build structure, and shape a practical system around what the work actually needs.'},
  {number:'03',stage:'Implement',image:'approach-implement.png',text:'Bring the system into practice through collaboration, documentation, enablement, and clear ownership.'},
  {number:'04',stage:'Improve',image:'approach-improve.png',text:'Measure what changed, learn from use, and refine the system so it continues creating value.'}
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Approach">
<section class="approach-v52"><div class="container">
  <div class="approach-v52-header"><div class="eyebrow">Approach</div><h1>From understanding the problem to building something that lasts.</h1><p>I use a simple four-part approach to move from ambiguity toward a system that is clear, usable, and capable of improving over time.</p></div>
  <div class="approach-flow">{stages.map(stage => <GrowthStage {...stage} />)}</div>
  <div class="approach-principle reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow">Design principle</div><p class="statement">Structure should make good judgment easier.</p></div><div><p>I don't believe the answer to complexity is more bureaucracy. Good systems create enough clarity, visibility, and shared language that people spend less energy reconstructing information and more energy making useful decisions.</p><p>Documentation has to be findable. Metrics have to lead somewhere. Processes have to reflect reality. And the people doing the work have to be part of the design.</p></div></div>
</div></section></BaseLayout>
